invariant: INV-16
file: srv_auth.c
catches: hash_runtime_exporter_test
reason: srv_hash_signed_content hashes a CertificateVerify's signed
  content on sha256.c whatever the session's ch_cfg.cpu states, so a
  server that stated the SHA-256 instructions runs that hash on the
  portable code. Every signature is the same, because both paths
  compute the same digest, so no vector fails.
  bin/hash_runtime_exporter_test's srv_hash_signed_content row counts
  the calls on the wrong path.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    sha256_update_cpu(cpu, &s, content, SRV_SIGNED_PAD_LEN + sizeof srv_cv_context + hash_len);
    sha256_final_cpu(cpu, &s, out);
#else
--- new
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    (void)cpu;
    sha256_update(&s, content, SRV_SIGNED_PAD_LEN + sizeof srv_cv_context + hash_len);
    sha256_final(&s, out);
#else
